Verse 1:
[G]'Tis so sweet to [C]trust in [G]Jesus, Just to take him [A]at his [D]word;
[G]Just to rest up[C]on his [G]promise, Just to [C]know, "Thus [D]saith the [G]Lord."
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [D]how I trust him! [G]How I've proved him [A]o'er and [D]o'er!
[G]Jesus, Jesus, [C]precious [G]Jesus! O for [C]grace to [D]trust him [G]more!

Refrain:
[G]Jesus, [C]Jesus, [G]how [A]I [D]trust him!
[G]How [C]I've [G]proved [C]him [D]o'er [G]and o'er!
[G][D]Jesus, [G]Jesus, [A]precious [D]Jesus!
[G]O [C]for [G]grace [C]to [D]trust [G]him more!

Verse 2:
[G]O [C]how [G]sweet to [A]trust [D]in Jesus,
[G]just [C]to [G]trust [C]his [D]cleansing [G]blood;
[G]and [D]in [G]simple faith [A]to [D]plunge me
[G][C]neath [G]the [C]healing, [D]cleansing [G]flood!

Verse 3:
[G]Yes, [C]'tis [G]sweet to [A]trust [D]in Jesus,
[G]just [C]from [G]sin [C]and [D]self [G]to cease;
[G]just [D]from [G]Jesus [A]simply [D]taking
[G]life [C]and [G]rest, [C]and [D]joy [G]and peace.

Verse 4:
[G]I'm [C]so glad [G]I [A]learned to [D]trust thee,
[G][C]precious [G]Jesus, [C][D]Savior, [G]friend;
[G]and [D]I know [G]that [A]thou art [D]with me,
[G]wilt [C]be [G]with [C]me [D]to [G]the end.
